Every modality is normalized per band with statistics computed on the pretraining corpus itself, because the default OlmoEarth statistics come from another corpus;
for Sentinel-1 they differ strongly. The Core-S2L2A statistics are the per-band means and standard deviations stored in the OlmoEarth normalization configuration ( computed.json , patched for this corpus); the Elliot-Pretrain statistics are elliot_band_stats.json next to the three partitions,
computed over valid pixels of 2,000 Monotemporal tiles with one 352-pixel window each, and the same statistics are applied to the Monthly and Burst tiles. The transform is the z-score ( x − μ ) / σ (x-\mu)/\sigma .
Sentinel-1 backscatter is first converted from linear power to dB and its statistics are VV − 11.42 ± 4.79 -11.42\pm 4.79 dB and VH − 17.89 ± 4.85 -17.89\pm 4.85 dB, computed over the valid pixels of 2,000 random Monotemporal tiles (seed 0), one 352-pixel window each, of the released layer.
